    {
      "text": "A link invariant from quantum dilogarithm — The link invariant, arising from the cyclic quantum dilogarithm via the particular R-matrix construction, is proved to coincide with the invariant of\n\n**A link invariant from quantum dilogarithm**\n\n*R.M. Kashaev∗*\n\n10 pp, 6 sections.\n\n**Abstract.** The link invariant, arising from the cyclic quantum dilogarithm via the particular R-matrix construction, is proved to coincide with the invariant of triangulated links in S3 introduced in [14]. The obtained invariant, like Alexander-Conway polynomial, vanishes on disjoint union of links. The R-matrix can be considered as the cyclic analog of the universal R-matrix associated with Uq(sl(2)) algebra. ENSLAPP-L-517/95 ∗On leave from St. Petersburg Branch of the Steklov Mathematical Institute, Fontanka 27, St. Petersburg 191011, RUSSIA †URA 14-36 du CNRS, associ´ee `a l’E.N.S. de Lyon, et `a l’Universit`e de Savoie\n\n**Outline.** Front matter; 1 Introduction; 2 The $R$-Matrix; 3 Invariants of Links in Three-Sphere; 4 Three-Dimensional Description; 5 Summary",
      "lang": "en",
